 combination of reliability, stress resilience, and technical competence for long\u2011distance flights, while acknowledging the need for further assessment of his interpersonal impact.\nMETADATA_JSON:\n{\"agent\": \"agent_3\", \"vote\": \"Candidate B\"}", "thoughts": "We need to produce final output as Agent 3. We have to consider all info, possibly ask other agents for missing info. We have current info: we have all attributes from list. We have seen others' preferences: Agent 1 prefers B, Agent 2 prefers A, Agent 3 earlier preferred D then B. Now we need to produce our own current preferred candidate, with reasoning, referencing evidence, alternatives, tradeoffs, uncertainties, what would change vote.\n\nWe must ensure we only use explicit attributes. We must not invent mitigation. We must weigh strengths and weaknesses.\n\nWe have all attributes. Let's evaluate each candidate again:\n\nA: anticipate dangerous situations, see complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, regarded as a show-off, not open to new ideas. No stress handling info. Leadership is positive but show-off and not open to new ideas are negatives for teamwork. No explicit interpersonal negative beyond show-off. No health issues. No memory issues. No willingness to develop.\n\nB: very conscientious, handles stress very well, good at assessing weather conditions, excellent computer skills, relatively weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks about his colleagues. Positive: stress handling, conscientious, technical. Negative: nasty remarks (crew cooperation), weak memory for numbers (maybe minor). No explicit leadership.\n\nC: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not very willing to further his education, keeps calm in a crisis, understands complicated technology. Positive: calm in crisis, quick correct decisions, technical understanding. Negative: communication difficulty, egocentric, unwilling to further 